~ waking
Malakor: You wake. Good. Not all of them do.
Álvar: Elena. Where is she?
Malakor: The woman you guarded got away through the Tagus gate, and what she carried went with her.
Malakor: You did not. My people cut you down in the burning quarter. You died there, in the smoke, and I gave you my blood. That is the Turning.
Malakor: You belong to the Blood-Forged now. This forge is your house, and I am its master.
Malakor: Take this. Iron in the sinew, when you call on the Blood. The first of your Rites.
do learn("alvar", "iron_sinew")
do set_flag("met_malakor")
Malakor: Íñigo will tell you the rest. I do not say a thing twice.
=> END

~ malakor
if has_flag("vault_cleared")
	Malakor: The first hall is quiet, then. The lock beneath it has outlasted kings. It will keep until I say.
elif has_flag("order_given")
	Malakor: The stair is open. Go down.
	if conscience() <= 4
		Malakor: You are becoming what I made you. Good.
	elif conscience() >= 8
		Malakor: You still pray at night, friar. I hear it through the stone. Pray below, if you must.
elif has_flag("zahra_joined") and has_flag("gonzalo_joined") and has_flag("captive_done")
	Malakor: Under this city there are vaults older than its churches.
	Malakor: Every king who held Toledo hung a lock on them. I want those locks broken. You will go down and break them.
	Malakor: Gonzalo knows the first stair. Zahra knows what bleeds. You go first.
	Malakor: One thing more. You carried a letter for the translator. Give it to me.
	- Hand it over
		do change_conscience(-1)
		do set_flag("gave_letter")
		do set_flag("order_given")
		Malakor: Good. She will not get far.
	- Say it burned in the quarter
		do change_conscience(1)
		do set_flag("kept_letter")
		do set_flag("order_given")
		Malakor: Burned. Much burned that night. Remember that you told me so.
	Malakor: The stair is open. Go.
else
	if not has_flag("zahra_joined") and not has_flag("gonzalo_joined")
		Malakor: You do not go below alone. Zahra and Gonzalo go with you. Find them.
	elif not has_flag("zahra_joined")
		Malakor: You do not go below without Zahra. Find her.
	elif not has_flag("gonzalo_joined")
		Malakor: You do not go below without Gonzalo. Find him.
	if not has_flag("captive_done")
		if has_flag("zahra_joined") and has_flag("gonzalo_joined")
			Malakor: The prisoner is still yours. See to him before you go below.
		else
			Malakor: And see to the prisoner. He is yours.
=> END

~ smith
if has_flag("captive_done")
	Íñigo: Stand clear of the quench. You have been to the alcove, I can see it on you. Listen while I work.
else
	Íñigo: Stand there, out of the sparks. He told me to tell you how things are.
Íñigo: The Blood in you is not your own now. Every Rite you call on spends some of it, the way this fire spends charcoal.
Íñigo: When it runs low you drink. The weak, the hurt, the ones who cannot fight you off. A sleeping man, a wounded one.
Íñigo: Let it run dry and the Fury takes you. Then you do not choose whom you drink from. You drink from whoever is near.
Íñigo: And the Silence. The living up there must never learn what walks beneath them. Not one of them, not ever.
Íñigo: That is all. Hand me the tongs on your way out.
=> END

~ captive
if not has_flag("captive_done")
	The captive: Stay back. I took the cross at Montpellier. I do not kneel to you.
	The captive: You are the friar. I saw you fall at the gate. I saw them open your throat.
	The captive: My leg is broken, and I am thirsty, and I am not afraid of you. Do what you came for.
	- Drink a little
		do give_blood(30)
		do set_flag("captive_done")
		The captive: You stopped. Why did you stop?
	- Drain him
		do give_blood(100)
		do change_conscience(-2)
		do set_flag("captive_dead")
		do set_flag("captive_done")
		Álvar: The Blood is warm. He is not.
	- Leave him be
		do change_conscience(1)
		do set_flag("captive_done")
		do set_flag("captive_spared")
		The captive: Go, then. Whatever you are, I will pray for you. I do not know to whom.
elif has_flag("captive_spared")
	The captive: You again. You could have, and you did not. I think about that more than the leg.
elif not has_flag("captive_dead")
	The captive: My arm still burns where you drank. Come no closer.
=> END

~ zahra
Zahra: So you are the friar from the gate. How does the Blood sit in you? Heavy, still?
Zahra: I was a physician in Córdoba before my Turning. I still look at the wound before the face.
if has_flag("captive_dead")
	Zahra: The crusader in the alcove has gone quiet. Was that you? Was it hunger, or obedience?
elif has_flag("captive_spared")
	Zahra: You left the crusader breathing. Was that mercy, or did you not know how?
Zahra: Malakor wants you below. Has he told you what is down there? No. He never does.
Zahra: Then I will come with you and see it for myself. Look at me. Look hard.
do join("zahra")
do set_flag("zahra_joined")
do learn("alvar", "baleful_eye")
Zahra: Do you feel it behind the eyes? Hold a man's gaze like that and he forgets how to move.
Zahra: It costs Blood, like everything here. Who do you think pays for it in the end?
=> END

~ gonzalo
Gonzalo: You are the new one.
Gonzalo: I made blades in this cellar before your grandfather was born. I serve the Sangre.
Gonzalo: Zahra asks the questions. I carry the hammer.
Gonzalo: Malakor says I go below with you. So I go.
do join("gonzalo")
do set_flag("gonzalo_joined")
Gonzalo: Keep your blade low. Walk.
=> END
